  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B2C43F">Remark <span data-tag="B2C43F">8.1.5.3</span>.</a>$S$-tree!associated Let $\calC $ be a presentable category, $S$ a collection of morphisms in $\calC $, and $\{  Y_{\alpha } \} _{ \alpha in A}$ an $S$-tree in $\calC $ with root $X$. Given a map $f: X \rightarrow X'$, we can form an <em>associated $S$-tree</em> $ \{  Y_{\alpha } \coprod _{X} X' \} _{\alpha \in A}$, having root $X'$. </p>
